    "narrative": "Our lineup construction for today reflects a strategic pivot toward capitalizing on favorable matchups against high-xERA arms, headlined by **Lawrence Butler**, who commands the highest score of the day at 70.69. **Butler** is poised for a breakout performance against Ure\u00f1a, benefiting from a massive 13% boost due to his dynamic platoon advantage. Similarly, **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02) are prime candidates for high-floor production; they are perfectly positioned to exploit a favorable wind out and a weak matchup against L\u00f3pez, whose 5.26 xERA provides a significant cushion for our leadoff and middle-order bats. We also see high-leverage value from **Cal Raleigh** (68.39), whose ability to hit third against the lefty Cantillo allows him to maximize his dynamic platoon edge and favorable spot in the order.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Gavin Sheets**, who narrowly missed the elite-tier scoring bracket with a 58.94. While **Sheets** benefits from a healthy 14% boost against Sasaki, he ultimately remained on the lower end of our starting rotation because we prioritized the high-ceiling output of **Jonathan Aranda** (66.14). **Aranda** secures his spot in the UTIL slot thanks to an impressive 0.373 xwOBA and a 12% platoon bump against Gallen. We remain concerned about the marginal scores of **Masyn Winn** (44.89) and **Daulton Varsho** (49.44), both of whom are facing difficult SP matchups; **Winn** is hampered by his 6th-order slot and opposing pitcher skill, while **Varsho** is facing Eovaldi, an elite arm that suppresses his efficiency despite the platoon advantage. \n\nWe continue to monitor the absence of our star core, as **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Dylan Beavers** remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us reliant on depth pieces like **Geraldo Perdomo** (61.12) to stabilize our counting stats. While the current lineup lacks the explosive upside of **Brendan Donovan** or **Gleyber Torres**\u2014who remain in our depth considerations\u2014we believe the combination of **Taylor Ward**\u2019s park-adjusted power and **Yainer Diaz**\u2019s strong recent form provides the necessary velocity to compete in today's 5x5 matchups. Keep a close eye on the weather and the pending status for **Masyn Winn**; if the defensive environment shifts, we are prepared to cycle in our bench reserves to protect our daily game caps.",
